IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): RELATED PROVISIONS of 2012, c. 19, ss. 251 to 270 (src:3694-3761),
-- the transition from boards of referees and umpires to the Social Security Tribunal.
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Seat: the person who has lost work and has an appeal or a request for reconsideration that was pending on
-- April 1, 2013. Sections 263 and 264 (the tenure of board chairpersons, panel members and umpires) are `inert`
-- in the coverage table and have no rule here; NOTES.md says why.
-- The dates are the Act's own; a day that an order under subsection 263(4) may fix earlier is a MAYBE DATE input.

§ `Section 251 - the bodies defined`

-- Each definition is worked out from the facts it names, as the keel does for section 2(1). The result of each is
-- a yes or no: this is a body the section defines. The constructors of `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision
-- about appeals` give the same bodies a name to return.
-- src:3694 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 251
-- src:3695 | Definitions
-- src:3696 | 251 The following definitions apply in sections 252 to 270.
-- src:3697 | board of referees means a board of referees established under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247. (conseil arbitral)
-- src:3698 | Pension Appeals Board means the Pension Appeals Board established under section 83 of the Canada Pension Plan, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 229. (Commission d’appel des pensions)
-- src:3699 | Review Tribunal means a Review Tribunal established under section 82 of the Canada Pension Plan, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 229. (tribunal de révision)
-- src:3700 | Social Security Tribunal means the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act. (Tribunal de la sécurité sociale)
-- src:3701 | umpire means an umpire appointed under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247. (juge-arbitre)
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 "board of referees" (src:3697)
GIVEN `it is a board of referees established under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is as that Part read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 251 board of referees` IF
        `it is a board of referees established under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act`
    AND `it is as that Part read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 "Pension Appeals Board" (src:3698)
GIVEN `it is the Pension Appeals Board established under section 83 of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is as that section read immediately before the coming into force of section 229` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 251 Pension Appeals Board` IF
        `it is the Pension Appeals Board established under section 83 of the Canada Pension Plan`
    AND `it is as that section read immediately before the coming into force of section 229`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 "Review Tribunal" (src:3699)
GIVEN `it is a Review Tribunal established under section 82 of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is as that section read immediately before the coming into force of section 229` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 251 Review Tribunal` IF
        `it is a Review Tribunal established under section 82 of the Canada Pension Plan`
    AND `it is as that section read immediately before the coming into force of section 229`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 "Social Security Tribunal" (src:3700)
GIVEN `it is the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 251 Social Security Tribunal` IF
    `it is the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 "umpire" (src:3701)
GIVEN `it is an umpire appointed under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is as that Part read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 251 umpire` IF
        `it is an umpire appointed under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act`
    AND `it is as that Part read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`

§ `Section 252 - information to be transferred to the Social Security Tribunal`

-- A duty of four former bodies, owed to the Tribunal: the person whose application the Tribunal is seized of holds no
-- claim under it. The duty arises for information that relates to an application of which the Tribunal is seized OR
-- that the Governor in Council has, by regulation, prescribed.
-- src:3703 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 252
-- src:3704 | Information
-- src:3705 | 252 The Pension Appeals Board, a Review Tribunal, a board of referees or an umpire must transfer to the Social Security Tribunal any information under their control that either relates to an application of which that Tribunal is seized or that the Governor in Council has, by regulation, prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 252 (src:3705)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
      `the information relates to an application of which the Social Security Tribunal is seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor in Council has, by regulation, prescribed the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 252 the body must transfer the information to the Social Security Tribunal` IF
        (   `the body` EQUALS `ei7 the Pension Appeals Board`
         OR `the body` EQUALS `ei7 a Review Tribunal`
         OR `the body` EQUALS `ei7 the board of referees`
         OR `the body` EQUALS `ei7 an umpire`)
    AND (   `the information relates to an application of which the Social Security Tribunal is seized`
         OR `the Governor in Council has, by regulation, prescribed the information`)

§ `Section 265 - appeals to the board of referees`

-- (1) remains seized of an appeal filed under the old subsection 114(1) and not decided before April 1, 2013.
-- "Filed ... before April 1, 2013" is read with "not decided before April 1, 2013": the old subsection 114(1) was
-- repealed with section 247, so no appeal could be filed under it later. Fork F5.
-- src:3723 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 265
-- src:3724 | Appeals — board of referees
-- src:3725 | 265 (1) The board of referees remains seized of any appeal filed and not decided before April 1, 2013 under subsection 114(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247.
-- src:3726 | Time limit
-- src:3727 | (2) The board of referees must make its decision no later than October 31, 2013 or, if an order is made under subsection 263(4), the day before the day fixed by that order.
-- src:3728 | Failure to decide
-- src:3729 | (3) The General Division of the Social Security Tribunal becomes seized of any appeal referred to in subsection (1) if no decision has been made by the day referred to in subsection (2). The appeal is deemed to be an appeal filed with the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal on November 1, 2013 or, if an order is made under subsection 263(4), the day fixed by that order.
-- src:3730 | Appeals — Social Security Tribunal
-- src:3731 | (4) A person who is dissatisfied with a decision made under subsection (1) may appeal the decision to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(1) (src:3725)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013` MEANS YMD 2013 4 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(2) (src:3727)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(2) October 31, 2013` MEANS YMD 2013 10 31

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(3) (src:3729)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) November 1, 2013` MEANS YMD 2013 11 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(1) (src:3725)
GIVEN `the appeal was filed under subsection 114(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 114(1) or 115(1) as they read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `the day on which the appeal was filed` IS A DATE
      `the appeal was decided before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(1) the board of referees remains seized of the appeal` IF
        `the appeal was filed under subsection 114(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`
    AND `the day on which the appeal was filed` LESS THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`
    AND (NOT `the appeal was decided before April 1, 2013`)

-- (2) the board must decide no later than October 31, 2013 or, if an order is made under subsection 263(4), the day
-- before the day fixed by that order. "No later than" includes the day itself. Fork F6.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(2) (src:3727)
GIVEN `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)` IS A MAYBE DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(2) the last day on which the board of referees must make its decision` IS
    CONSIDER `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(2) October 31, 2013`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed MINUS 1

-- (3) if no decision has been made by that day, the General Division becomes seized of the appeal, which is deemed
-- an appeal filed with the General Division on November 1, 2013 or, if an order is made under subsection 263(4), the
-- day fixed by that order. A decision made after the last day is no decision "by the day".
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(3) (src:3729)
GIVEN `the appeal was filed under subsection 114(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 114(1) or 115(1) as they read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `the day on which the appeal was filed` IS A DATE
      `the appeal was decided before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the board of referees made its decision` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)` IS A MAYBE DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) the body that becomes seized of the appeal` IS
    IF     `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(1) the board of referees remains seized of the appeal` `the appeal was filed under subsection 114(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` `the day on which the appeal was filed` `the appeal was decided before April 1, 2013`
       AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the board of referees made its decision`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST decided THEN decided GREATER THAN (`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(2) the last day on which the board of referees must make its decision` `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)`))
    THEN JUST `ei7 the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(3) (src:3729)
GIVEN `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)` IS A MAYBE DATE  -- out of range: a day fixed by order or by another section of the amending Act; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) the day on which the appeal is deemed to have been filed with the General Division` IS
    CONSIDER `the day fixed by an order made under subsection 263(4)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(3) November 1, 2013`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed

-- (4) a person dissatisfied with a decision made under subsection (1) may appeal it to the Appeal Division.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 265(4) (src:3731)
GIVEN `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was made under subsection 265(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265(4) the body to which the person may appeal the decision` IS
    IF `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` AND `the decision was made under subsection 265(1)`
    THEN JUST `ei7 the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 266 - an appeal that could have gone to an umpire`

-- src:3733 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 266
-- src:3734 | Appeals — umpire
-- src:3735 | 266 An appeal from a decision of a board of referees that could have been appealed to an umpire, but for the repeal of subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act by section 247, may be appealed to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 266 (src:3735)
GIVEN `it is an appeal from a decision of a board of referees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could have been appealed to an umpire but for the repeal of subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act by section 247` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 266 the body to which the appeal may be appealed` IS
    IF `it is an appeal from a decision of a board of referees`
       AND `it could have been appealed to an umpire but for the repeal of subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act by section 247`
    THEN JUST `ei7 the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 267 - appeals to an umpire`

-- (1) an umpire remains seized of an appeal filed and heard before April 1, 2013 under the old subsection 115(1).
-- src:3737 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 267
-- src:3738 | Appeals — umpire
-- src:3739 | 267 (1) An umpire remains seized of any appeal filed and heard before April 1, 2013 under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247.
-- src:3740 | Time limit
-- src:3741 | (2) An umpire must make his or her decision no later than March 31, 2014.
-- src:3742 | Failure to decide
-- src:3743 | (3) The Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal becomes seized of any appeal referred to in subsection (1) if no decision has been made by the day referred to in subsection (2). The Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal is deemed to have granted leave to appeal on April 1, 2014.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267 (src:3741)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(2) March 31, 2014` MEANS YMD 2014 3 31

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267(3) (src:3743)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) April 1, 2014` MEANS YMD 2014 4 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267(1) (src:3739)
GIVEN `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 114(1) or 115(1) as they read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `the day on which the appeal was filed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal was heard` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(1) the umpire remains seized of the appeal` IF
        `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`
    AND `the day on which the appeal was filed` LESS THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the appeal was heard`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST heard THEN heard LESS THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`)

-- (2) the umpire must decide no later than March 31, 2014 (that day included).
-- (3) if no decision has been made by that day the Appeal Division becomes seized and is deemed to have granted leave
-- to appeal on April 1, 2014.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267(2) (src:3741)
GIVETH A DATE
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(2) the last day on which the umpire must make the decision` MEANS `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(2) March 31, 2014`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267(3) (src:3743)
GIVEN `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 114(1) or 115(1) as they read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `the day on which the appeal was filed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appeal was heard` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the umpire made the decision` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) the Appeal Division becomes seized of the appeal` IF
        `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(1) the umpire remains seized of the appeal` `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` `the day on which the appeal was filed` `the day on which the appeal was heard`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the umpire made the decision`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST decided THEN decided GREATER THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(2) the last day on which the umpire must make the decision`)

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 267(3) (src:3743)
GIVEN `the Appeal Division has become seized of the appeal under subsection 267(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) the day on which the Appeal Division is deemed to have granted leave to appeal` IS
    IF `the Appeal Division has become seized of the appeal under subsection 267(3)`
    THEN JUST `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 267(3) April 1, 2014`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 268 - appeals not yet heard on April 1, 2013`

-- src:3745 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 268
-- src:3746 | Appeals — Social Security Tribunal
-- src:3747 | 268 The Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal is deemed to have granted leave to appeal on April 1, 2013 with respect to any appeal filed and not heard before April 1, 2013 under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 268 (src:3747)
GIVEN `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 114(1) or 115(1) as they read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `the day on which the appeal was filed` IS A DATE
      `the appeal was heard before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 268 the day on which the Appeal Division is deemed to have granted leave to appeal` IS
    IF     `the appeal was filed under subsection 115(1) of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`
       AND `the day on which the appeal was filed` LESS THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`
       AND (NOT `the appeal was heard before April 1, 2013`)
    THEN JUST `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 269 - requests for reconsideration`

-- (1)(a), (b) and (2)(a), (b) give the same pairing: a decision of a board of referees is treated as one of the General
-- Division, and a decision of an umpire as one of the Appeal Division. Any other body: the section says nothing.
-- src:3749 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 269
-- src:3750 | Request for reconsideration
-- src:3751 | 269 (1) If no decision has been made before April 1, 2013 in respect of a request made under section 120 of the Employment Insurance Act as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247, it is deemed to be an application made on April 1, 2013 under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act and is deemed to relate to a decision made, as the case may be, by
-- src:3752 | (a) the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal, in the case of a decision made by a board of referees; or
-- src:3753 | (b) the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, in the case of a decision made by an umpire.
-- src:3754 | Deeming
-- src:3755 | (2) An application made under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act after March 31, 2013 is deemed to relate to a decision made, as the case may be, by
-- src:3756 | (a) the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal, in the case of a decision made by a board of referees; or
-- src:3757 | (b) the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, in the case of a decision made by an umpire.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 269(1)(a), (b), (2)(a), (b) (src:3752-3753) (src:3756-3757)
GIVEN `the decision was made by` IS A `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269 the division of the Social Security Tribunal whose decision the application is deemed to relate to` IS
    CONSIDER `the decision was made by`
    WHEN `ei7 the board of referees` THEN JUST `ei7 the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    WHEN `ei7 an umpire` THEN JUST `ei7 the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 269(1) (src:3751)
GIVEN `a request was made under section 120 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 120 as it read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `a decision was made on the request before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(1) the day on which the request is deemed to have been made as an application under section 66` IS
    IF     `a request was made under section 120 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`
       AND (NOT `a decision was made on the request before April 1, 2013`)
    THEN JUST `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 265 April 1, 2013`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 269(1) (src:3751-3753)
GIVEN `a request was made under section 120 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 120 as it read before section 247, repealed (piece ei4)
      `a decision was made on the request before April 1, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was made by` IS A `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(1) the division whose decision the deemed application relates to` IS
    IF     `a request was made under section 120 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247`
       AND (NOT `a decision was made on the request before April 1, 2013`)
    THEN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269 the division of the Social Security Tribunal whose decision the application is deemed to relate to` `the decision was made by`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 269(2) (src:3755)
`Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(2) March 31, 2013` MEANS YMD 2013 3 31

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 269(2) (src:3755-3757)
GIVEN `the day on which the application was made under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act` IS A DATE
      `the decision was made by` IS A `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals`
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(2) the division whose decision the application is deemed to relate to` IS
    IF `the day on which the application was made under section 66 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269(2) March 31, 2013`
    THEN `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 269 the division of the Social Security Tribunal whose decision the application is deemed to relate to` `the decision was made by`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 270 - continued application of the repealed provisions`

-- "with any necessary adaptations": the adaptations are not stated, so the rule says only that the repealed
-- provisions and their related regulations continue to apply, not what they say.
-- src:3759 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 270
-- src:3760 | Continued application
-- src:3761 | 270 The provisions of the Employment Insurance Act repealed by this Act, and their related regulations, continue to apply to appeals of which the board of referees or an umpire remains seized under this Act, with any necessary adaptations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2012, c. 19, s. 270 (src:3761)
GIVEN `the board of referees or an umpire remains seized of the appeal under 2012, c. 19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2012 c. 19 s. 270 the provisions repealed by that Act and their related regulations continue to apply to the appeal` IF
    `the board of referees or an umpire remains seized of the appeal under 2012, c. 19`
